1
00:00:00,450 --> 00:00:04,059
A football rolling slowly is
easy to stop with your foot.

2
00:00:04,059 --> 00:00:06,487
A car rolling just as slowly is not.

3
00:00:06,887 --> 00:00:09,455
And a fast cricket ball stings your hands.

4
00:00:09,455 --> 00:00:12,223
So what decides how
hard a thing is to stop?

5
00:00:12,673 --> 00:00:14,784
Diya waits at the college gate.

6
00:00:14,784 --> 00:00:16,641
A loaded truck creeps past.

7
00:00:16,641 --> 00:00:19,357
Inside, a cricket ball flies off a bat.

8
00:00:19,707 --> 00:00:21,827
The ball is forty times faster.

9
00:00:21,827 --> 00:00:23,594
The truck is far heavier.

10
00:00:23,594 --> 00:00:25,567
Which one is harder to stop?

11
00:00:26,067 --> 00:00:27,914
Speed alone cannot tell you.

12
00:00:27,914 --> 00:00:29,563
Mass alone cannot either.

13
00:00:29,563 --> 00:00:31,259
You need both, together.

14
00:00:31,909 --> 00:00:34,000
That combination has a name.

15
00:00:34,000 --> 00:00:34,900
Momentum.

16
00:00:35,165 --> 00:00:38,066
Momentum, p, is mass times velocity.

17
00:00:38,066 --> 00:00:39,334
p equals m v.

18
00:00:39,734 --> 00:00:42,061
Kilograms times metres per second.

19
00:00:42,061 --> 00:00:45,143
So momentum is in kilogram
metres per second.

20
00:00:45,543 --> 00:00:48,708
Velocity has a direction,
so momentum does too.

21
00:00:48,708 --> 00:00:51,922
More mass, or more speed,
means more momentum.

22
00:00:52,322 --> 00:00:54,690
Newton called it the quantity of motion.

23
00:00:55,340 --> 00:00:56,836
To the motion notebook.

24
00:00:56,836 --> 00:01:00,786
A half kilogram ball and a two
kilogram cart, on a smooth floor.

25
00:01:01,136 --> 00:01:03,495
Both move at two metres per second.

26
00:01:03,495 --> 00:01:06,301
The ball has one kilogram
metre per second.

27
00:01:06,301 --> 00:01:07,656
The cart has four.

28
00:01:08,056 --> 00:01:10,654
Each body has its own line on the graph.

29
00:01:10,654 --> 00:01:13,047
The heavier body has the steeper line.

30
00:01:13,047 --> 00:01:14,583
The slope is the mass.

31
00:01:14,983 --> 00:01:18,076
Now send the ball at
eight metres per second.

32
00:01:18,076 --> 00:01:20,061
Its momentum climbs to four.

33
00:01:20,061 --> 00:01:21,414
Exactly the cart's.

34
00:01:21,814 --> 00:01:24,790
Four times lighter, but four times faster.

35
00:01:24,790 --> 00:01:25,900
Same momentum.

36
00:01:26,500 --> 00:01:27,608
Slow-mo replay.

37
00:01:27,608 --> 00:01:29,732
Freeze, and draw the arrows.

38
00:01:30,082 --> 00:01:32,795
The blue velocity arrows
are very different.

39
00:01:32,795 --> 00:01:36,048
Times the mass, the momentum
arrows come out equal.

40
00:01:36,648 --> 00:01:39,265
Now stop both, in the same half a second.

41
00:01:39,665 --> 00:01:42,455
The orange stopping forces are equal too.

42
00:01:42,455 --> 00:01:43,871
Eight newtons each.

43
00:01:43,871 --> 00:01:46,599
Same momentum, same time, same force.

44
00:01:47,249 --> 00:01:51,431
Now let's link momentum to Newton's
second law, one step at a time.

45
00:01:51,781 --> 00:01:52,819
Step one.

46
00:01:52,819 --> 00:01:54,910
Momentum p equals m v.

47
00:01:55,660 --> 00:01:56,598
Step two.

48
00:01:56,598 --> 00:02:01,759
From episode fifty two, F equals
m a, and a equals d v by d t.

49
00:02:02,509 --> 00:02:03,625
Step three.

50
00:02:03,625 --> 00:02:08,819
With the mass fixed, m d v by
d t equals d by d t of m v.

51
00:02:08,819 --> 00:02:10,784
That is d p by d t.

52
00:02:11,534 --> 00:02:12,515
Step four.

53
00:02:12,515 --> 00:02:14,634
So F equals d p by d t.

54
00:02:14,634 --> 00:02:18,004
Net force is the rate
of change of momentum.

55
00:02:18,754 --> 00:02:19,655
Step five.

56
00:02:19,655 --> 00:02:23,881
For a steady force, F equals
the change in p over the time.

57
00:02:23,881 --> 00:02:26,761
Four over half a second is eight newtons.

58
00:02:27,511 --> 00:02:31,238
So F equals m a is the
special case of fixed mass.

59
00:02:31,238 --> 00:02:35,320
And one newton second equals
one kilogram metre per second.

60
00:02:35,920 --> 00:02:37,007
Remember this.

61
00:02:37,007 --> 00:02:39,779
Force is the rate of change of momentum.

62
00:02:40,479 --> 00:02:41,557
Side by side.

63
00:02:41,557 --> 00:02:45,403
The truck: ten thousand kilograms
at one metre per second.

64
00:02:45,403 --> 00:02:48,009
Ten thousand kilogram metres per second.

65
00:02:48,409 --> 00:02:53,048
The ball: zero point one six
kilograms, at forty metres per second.

66
00:02:53,048 --> 00:02:54,578
Just six point four.

67
00:02:55,178 --> 00:02:56,236
Now you try.

68
00:02:56,236 --> 00:02:58,353
Both must stop in one second.

69
00:02:58,353 --> 00:03:00,408
Which needs the bigger force?

70
00:03:00,408 --> 00:03:01,724
Pause and decide.

71
00:03:04,924 --> 00:03:06,395
The truck, by far!

72
00:03:06,395 --> 00:03:09,437
Same time, so the force
follows the momentum.

73
00:03:09,437 --> 00:03:12,420
Ten thousand newtons,
against six point four.

74
00:03:13,070 --> 00:03:14,626
Now, the direction part.

75
00:03:14,976 --> 00:03:18,732
A two kilogram cart rolls east
at three metres per second.

76
00:03:18,732 --> 00:03:20,299
Take east as positive.

77
00:03:20,299 --> 00:03:21,473
p is plus six.

78
00:03:21,873 --> 00:03:22,954
Send it west.

79
00:03:22,954 --> 00:03:24,195
p is minus six.

80
00:03:24,195 --> 00:03:26,287
Same size, opposite direction.

81
00:03:26,287 --> 00:03:27,768
A different momentum.

82
00:03:28,368 --> 00:03:29,308
Your turn.

83
00:03:29,308 --> 00:03:34,029
Two kilograms east at three metres
per second, or three kilograms west

84
00:03:34,029 --> 00:03:34,929
at two.

85
00:03:34,806 --> 00:03:35,962
Same momentum?

86
00:03:35,962 --> 00:03:37,345
Pause and decide.

87
00:03:40,545 --> 00:03:41,445
No!

88
00:03:41,019 --> 00:03:45,020
Both have a size of six, but
plus six is not minus six.

89
00:03:45,670 --> 00:03:47,405
Now, one worked example.

90
00:03:47,755 --> 00:03:52,193
A twelve hundred kilogram van speeds
up from ten to twenty five metres

91
00:03:52,193 --> 00:03:54,140
per second in five seconds.

92
00:03:54,140 --> 00:03:57,461
Find the change in
momentum, and the net force.

93
00:03:57,961 --> 00:04:02,618
Starting momentum: twelve hundred times
ten, twelve thousand kilogram metres

94
00:04:02,618 --> 00:04:03,540
per second.

95
00:04:04,290 --> 00:04:08,561
Final momentum: twelve hundred
times twenty five, thirty thousand.

96
00:04:09,311 --> 00:04:13,161
So the change is eighteen thousand
kilogram metres per second.

97
00:04:13,911 --> 00:04:16,617
Force is the change in p over the time.

98
00:04:16,617 --> 00:04:20,655
Eighteen thousand over five, three
thousand six hundred newtons.

99
00:04:20,655 --> 00:04:23,450
Same as m a: twelve hundred times three.

100
00:04:24,100 --> 00:04:25,565
Now, the exam trap.

101
00:04:25,915 --> 00:04:30,219
A thousand kilogram car moves at
seventy two kilometres per hour.

102
00:04:30,219 --> 00:04:34,098
Many students write p equals
a thousand times seventy two.

103
00:04:34,498 --> 00:04:37,170
But speed must be in metres per second.

104
00:04:37,170 --> 00:04:39,932
Seventy two kilometres per hour is twenty.

105
00:04:39,932 --> 00:04:41,677
So p is twenty thousand.

106
00:04:42,327 --> 00:04:43,755
Where is this asked?

107
00:04:43,755 --> 00:04:47,358
In questions that find p or
its change, then the force.

108
00:04:47,958 --> 00:04:49,238
Exam level now.

109
00:04:49,238 --> 00:04:54,274
A two kilogram body has momentum p
equals four t squared, plus six t.

110
00:04:54,274 --> 00:04:57,898
Find the force and the
acceleration at two seconds.

111
00:04:57,898 --> 00:04:59,233
Pause and solve.

112
00:05:04,633 --> 00:05:05,934
The answer is A.

113
00:05:05,934 --> 00:05:09,707
Twenty two newtons, and eleven
metres per second squared.

114
00:05:10,207 --> 00:05:12,011
Force is d p by d t.

115
00:05:12,011 --> 00:05:14,183
That is eight t, plus six.

116
00:05:14,683 --> 00:05:18,910
At two seconds, eight times two,
plus six, is twenty two newtons.

117
00:05:19,410 --> 00:05:21,434
Then a is F over m, eleven.

118
00:05:21,434 --> 00:05:24,136
Twenty eight is p itself, not the force.

119
00:05:24,736 --> 00:05:26,201
Here is your recap.

120
00:05:26,201 --> 00:05:27,706
Screenshot this card.

121
00:05:30,906 --> 00:05:32,837
Can you answer these without help?

122
00:05:33,237 --> 00:05:34,137
One.

123
00:05:33,742 --> 00:05:37,821
A slow truck or a fast cricket
ball: which has more momentum?

124
00:05:38,721 --> 00:05:39,621
Two.

125
00:05:39,279 --> 00:05:41,251
Why is momentum a vector?

126
00:05:42,151 --> 00:05:43,051
Three.

127
00:05:42,895 --> 00:05:47,212
How does F equals d p by
d t become F equals m a?

128
00:05:48,112 --> 00:05:50,957
Next time: the same
egg, at the same speed.

129
00:05:50,957 --> 00:05:53,521
One catch breaks it, the other does not.

130
00:05:53,521 --> 00:05:54,421
Why?

131
00:05:53,983 --> 00:05:54,883
Impulse.
